<title>FRANCE: Majority of French see EMU on schedule - poll.</title>
<headline>Majority of French see EMU on schedule - poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A majority of the French people believe that France should and will be in the first wave of European nations adopting a single currency in 1999, according to a poll made public on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The BVA survey for French radio BFM found that 64 percent of French adults believed both that France would be among those joining Economic and Monetary Union from 1999 and that it was necessary that it do so.</p>
<p>In addition, 55 percent felt that monetary union would proceed on schedule, taking effect on January 1, 1999, as planned, according to the poll.</p>
<p>The poll surveyed 949 people aged 18 and over last Friday and Saturday. The margin of error was two to three percentage points in either direction, BVA said.</p>
<p>Following are poll details:</p>
